What happens as we keep more answers from the first model?
We choose and test these cutoffs on the same questions.
We replayed recorded answers on the 2,198 questions. Each first model answers the share of questions it is most confident about (x); the second model answers the rest. Grey line: the second model alone. Curves that use the same questions to choose and test can look better than a test on new questions; the main result uses separate halves.

